; prior: Python — `if 0:` skips the branch (0 is falsy).
; expectation: Loon DIVERGES: 0 is a value and therefore truthy, so the then
; arm runs. The divergence is LOUD: the checker's E0209 warning fires on the
; Int-typed condition and its fix text states the falsy-set rule.
; principle: diverge from a bad prior loudly at the point of divergence
; (agent-first.md P1/P2) — never silently.
; expect-stdout: zero-is-truthy
; expect-check: E0209
[fn main []
  [println [if 0 "zero-is-truthy" "zero-is-falsy"]]]
